     "explanation": "Adler is explicit that the pillars form a circuit with a specific order of enablement. A self that isn't accepted cannot genuinely extend trust (the 'trust' becomes grasping for validation). Trust enables contribution, because contributing requires believing the 'we' is real. Contribution then deepens self-acceptance, completing the loop. Option A misses the architecture. Option C is the productivity-first error — Adler explicitly warns against contributing from an unsteady self. Option D inverts the order; trust without a stable self collapses into approval-seeking.",
